*.run/
*.run.md
.temp/

# Benchmark inputs are regenerated deterministically by each pattern's
# inputs/gen.py (.memory/02-bench-rules.md); gen.py is committed, blobs are not.
patterns/*/inputs/*.bin
patterns-php/*/inputs/*.bin

__pycache__/
*.pyc

*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Diagnostic gate runs. `--skip`, `--no-build`, `--no-callgrind` and `--cells
# measured` all certify strictly less than a full run, so check.py writes them
# beside the full-run record rather than over it. Only the full-run record is
# committed evidence.
results/gate/*.partial.json
results-php/gate/*.partial.json

# ⚠⚠ `results-php/preflight/` IS COMMITTED. This block used to ignore the whole
# directory, on the rationale that the record "carries a `when` timestamp and
# the literal `gate_argv`, so it churns on every run". ⚠ That was measured and
# HALF WRONG (`TASK_PHP_005` F-2c, landed at `TASK_PHP_006`): across two
# identical runs only `when` moved -- `sha256(rest)` was `d91ce008ad273b36` both
# times -- and `gate_argv` is a function of the COMMAND, not of the run, which
# is exactly the evidence `TASK_PHP_003` M6 asked for. So `when` moved to the
# sidecar below and the record itself is committed evidence: it is the only
# place `harness_php_sha256` is recorded (`RECAP_PHP.md` open item 13), the only
# place a `--no-provenance` run leaves a trace, and the thing
# `gate.py --audit` checks for the presence of. ✅ Two identical
# `--preflight ph00` runs now leave it BYTE-IDENTICAL -- measured,
# `.temp/php6/09-f2-record.log`.
results-php/preflight/*.when.json

# `.web/` — the static report over this tree's evidence. It was ignored here and
# kept its own local git history until it was folded into this repository. Its
# own `.web/.gitignore` still drops the derived (`data/`, which
# `.web/build_data.py` rebuilds in about a second) and the ephemeral.